NAME
       sort - sort lines of text files

SYNOPSIS
       sort [OPTION]... [FILE]...

DESCRIPTION
       Write the sorted concatenation of all FILEs to standard output.

OPTIONS
       -r
           reverse the result

       -n
           compare by numeric value

       -h
           compare human readable numbers (2K, 1G)

       -V
           natural sort of version numbers

       -f
           fold lower case to upper case

       -b
           ignore leading blanks

       -u
           output only the first of equal lines

       -k N[,M][nrhf]
           sort by field N (to field M), with per-key options

       -t SEP
           use SEP as the field separator

       -o FILE
           write the result to FILE

       -c
           check whether input is sorted

EXAMPLES
       sort -n numbers.txt
       du -h /usr | sort -h
       sort -t: -k3n /etc/passwd

SEE ALSO
       uniq(1), cut(1)
